1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,800
Siguniang's peak is 6,250 m — altitude hits tourists far lower.
I'm your China Travel Expert

2
00:00:02,800 --> 00:00:05,200
This is Mount Siguniang — Sichuan's four snow "sister" peaks.

3
00:00:05,200 --> 00:00:07,600
Almost nobody climbs the 6,250 m main peak, Yaomei Feng.

4
00:00:07,600 --> 00:00:10,000
Most people walk the valleys — and that's the catch.

5
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:12,400
The base town, Rilong, already sits at 3,200 m.

6
00:00:12,400 --> 00:00:14,800
Trek toward Dafeng and you camp near 4,300 m.

7
00:00:14,800 --> 00:00:17,300
Double-tap if thin mountain air doesn't scare you off.

8
00:00:17,300 --> 00:00:19,800
Climb too fast and altitude sickness ends the trip.

9
00:00:19,800 --> 00:00:23,000
★ Expert Tip: sleep a night in Rilong first — acclimatize before the valleys.

10
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:26,000
Would you trek the high valley — or stay in the town below?
